The root cause is in [`sandbox-utils.ts` `generateProxyEnvVars()`](https://github.com/anthropic-experimental/sandbox-runtime/blob/433a67df/src/sandbox/sandbox-utils.ts#L279-L284). On macOS, `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` is set unconditionally with `nc -X 5`, even when `proxyAuthToken` is set:

```typescript
if (platform === 'macos') {
  // macOS: use BSD nc SOCKS5 proxy support (-X 5 -x). nc has no SOCKS5
  // auth, so when proxyAuthToken is set, git-over-ssh fails at the SOCKS
  // handshake — use git-over

I tried the workaround suggested by @cblecker , but it did not work for me. ~Instead, I found I needed to unset the env var:~  Actually, this is also not a viable workaround.

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "echo 'unset GIT_SSH_COMMAND' >> \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
